{
    "_comment": [
        "This file is the entire installation of the MTB features. It is mounted",
        "read-only into the official cBioPortal image and passed to it as",
        "--frontend.config. The portal serves it back to its own frontend through",
        "/config_service as frontendConfigOverride.",
        "",
        "'id' is NOT free-form. cBioPortal's router validates the tab id in the URL",
        "path, and a custom tab id must match one of the patterns in",
        "customTabParamValidator (src/routes.tsx at v6.4.4):",
        "  patient/openResource_.+   <- what we use",
        "  study/<StudyViewResourceTabPrefix>.+",
        "  .+/customTab[0-9]",
        "Any other id routes to an ErrorPage and the whole patient view goes blank.",
        "",
        "'unmountOnHide': true is deliberate -- it makes switching tabs actually",
        "unmount the tab, so the bundle's teardown path is exercised rather than",
        "left untested.",
        "",
        "Both tabs point at the same two files. custom_tabs loads one script per",
        "entry, and because the URL is identical the browser fetches it once; two",
        "separate bundles would each ship their own copy of React."
    ],
    "custom_tabs": [
        {
            "id": "openResource_mtbDemo",
            "title": "MTB Demo",
            "location": "PATIENT_PAGE",
            "mountCallbackName": "renderMtbDemoTab",
            "pathsToJs": ["__MTB_TOOLS_BASE_URL__/mtb-tools.js"],
            "pathsToCSS": ["__MTB_TOOLS_BASE_URL__/mtb-tools.css"],
            "customParameters": {},
            "unmountOnHide": true
        },
        {
            "_comment": [
                "Needs the risk overlay running:",
                "  docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f risk/docker-compose.yml up -d",
                "Without it the tab loads and reports that the service is",
                "unreachable, which is the intended behaviour rather than a blank",
                "panel.",
                "",
                "riskBaseUrl is the origin the BROWSER uses, not a compose service",
                "name. In this stack the service has its own port, so init.sh",
                "renders an absolute URL. Behind the auth proxy it would be '/risk'",
                "and share the portal's origin."
            ],
            "id": "openResource_mtbPrognosis",
            "title": "Prognosis",
            "location": "PATIENT_PAGE",
            "mountCallbackName": "renderMtbPrognosisTab",
            "pathsToJs": ["__MTB_TOOLS_BASE_URL__/mtb-tools.js"],
            "pathsToCSS": ["__MTB_TOOLS_BASE_URL__/mtb-tools.css"],
            "customParameters": {
                "riskBaseUrl": "__MTB_RISK_BASE_URL__",
                "apiBase": "/api"
            },
            "unmountOnHide": true
        }
    ]
}
